svn-fw-limited-load-external: TPM2_LoadExternal rejects firmwareLimited and svnLimited

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, version 185, TPMA_OBJECT, "Bit[8] -
*firmwareLimited*" and "Bit[9] - *svnLimited*"): "**External** | shall be
CLEAR" -- unconditionally, unlike *fixedTPM* ("if both public and sensitive
portions are loaded, shall be CLEAR").

The reference validates the attributes of an external object only when its
sensitive area is loaded (ObjectLoad() runs PublicAttributesValidation() only
with a sensitive area, where firmwareLimited/svnLimited then fail because
fixedTPM must be CLEAR), so it loads a public-only object with
firmwareLimited or svnLimited SET. tpm-rs rejects both attributes for every
external object with TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES + RC_LoadExternal_inPublic, after the
hierarchy and sensitive-area checks; the patch adds the same check to the
reference.
diff --git a/src/ObjectCommands.c b/src/ObjectCommands.c
--- a/src/ObjectCommands.c
+++ b/src/ObjectCommands.c
@@ -301,6 +301,13 @@ TPM2_LoadExternal(
 	    // initialization will load the sensitive part too
 	    sensitive = &in->inPrivate.sensitiveArea;
 	}
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // TPM 2.0 Part 2, TPMA_OBJECT Bit[8] firmwareLimited and Bit[9]
+    // svnLimited, "External: shall be CLEAR" (also for a public-only object,
+    // whose attributes ObjectLoad() does not validate).
+    if(IS_ATTRIBUTE(in->inPublic.publicArea.objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, firmwareLimited)
+       || IS_ATTRIBUTE(in->inPublic.publicArea.objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, svnLimited))
+	return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + RC_LoadExternal_inPublic;
     // Need the name to initialize the object structure
     PublicMarshalAndComputeName(&in->inPublic.publicArea, &out->name);
     // Load and validate key
